   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1158-opus-review, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES**, head 13d4c596\n\nThe fix itself is right. The test does not cover it: it stays green if the view change is removed.\n\n1. **Medium**: `App/SwiftHFRTests/Messages/MessageRowAvatarTests.swift:29-36` (the modifier is at `App/SwiftHFR/Messages/MessageRowView.swift:55`).\n   - **Failing scenario**: delete `.accessibilityValue(Self.accessibilityValue(of: thread))` at `MessageRowView.swift:55`. `groupRowIsSpoken` stays green, but VoiceOver no longer says anything about groups. The test only checks the static helper, never that the row uses it (LESSONS L01).\n   - **Spec gap**: #1158's \"Check\" asks for \"a hosted test that the combined row's accessibility text names the group\", and the diff has none.\n   - **Fix**: add a hosted assertion. The tools already exist: `HostedAccessibility.beginAutomation()` / `elements(under:)` (`App/SwiftHFRTests/Navigation/HostedHangWatchdog.swift:51`), and the Messages-tab host in `ListLookHostedTests` (dense on and off, so the experimental dense row is covered too). Give it a group row and check that the combined cell element's `accessibilityValue == \"Conversation de groupe\"` and that a one-to-one row has no value. Show it red without line 55.\n2. **Low**: `MessageRowAvatarTests.swift:33` checks against `row.isGroup`, but the code follows `avatarSubject(of:).isGroup`. A row with `isGroup == false` whose label is « Interlocuteurs multiples » (the label-only path, `multiplesLabel`) has no value case.\n   - **Fix**: add `#expect(MessageRowView.accessibilityValue(of: thread(starter: \"Interlocuteurs multiples\")) == \"Conversation de groupe\")`, which pins \"same rule as the icon\".\n\nChecked and correct:\n- **Accessibility tree**: none of the `.combine` row's children sets an accessibilityValue. The explicit value does not touch the combined label, so « non lu » / « Non lu par … » (the badge), « Non lu » (the circle), the title and the info line are still read, followed by « Conversation de groupe ».\n- **Empty value**: a one-to-one row's value is \"\", the same as the precedents (`AccountMenuButton.swift:50`, `LegacyTopicRowView.swift:52`).\n- **Dense row**: covered, because the modifier is on the shared outer `HStack`.\n- **Legacy pointer**: `MPListView.swift:775-787` @ 87fe0d1c is `interlocutorLabel`, which returns « Interlocuteurs multiples ». Correct.\n- **Fixture**: R13u1 has both group and one-to-one rows (`PrivateMessageListParserTests.swift:63`), and the test asserts both kinds exist.\n\n**Verified**:\n- fetched the branch and diffed it against origin/dev-swift;\n- read #1158 and legacy at 87fe0d1c;\n- ran `swiftlint lint --strict` on both files (0 violations, no line over 140 columns) in a throwaway worktree, since removed;\n- read the hosted-test tools.\n- Not done: no Xcode build, and no tests run.\n\nRound 1 fixed in 884052d (hosted test `MessageRowGroupHostedTests`, label-only case). Round 2 requested.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
