   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1158-opus-review, round 2) : APPROVE** — head 884052d6\n\nRound 1, finding 1 (no hosted test through the real row): fixed.\n- `MessageRowGroupHostedTests` puts the real `MessageRowView` in a plain `List`, inside a `UIHostingController` in a `UIWindow` of the connected scene, the same way as `FavorisHeaderTapHostedTests`.\n- It wraps the work in `HostedAccessibility.beginAutomation()`/`endAutomation()`, which use the reference-counted helper in `Navigation/HostedHangWatchdog.swift`. It then searches `HostedAccessibility.elements(under:)` for elements whose label contains `displayTitle`. Because the row is `.combine`, its combined element carries the title in its label.\n- `LiveTopicPageSourceTests.capture` is `static`, not private, and returns `Data`.\n- Every environment value the row reads is optional or has a default (`avatarRefresh`, `memberAvatars`, `ExperimentalSettings?`, `listDensity`, `textScale`). The memberwise init is already called from `MessageListView`.\n- Red without the change: without `.accessibilityValue`, the children carry no value (the avatar is `accessibilityHidden`, the texts have none), so no element gets « Conversation de groupe » and the group check fails.\n\nRound 1, finding 2 (no label-only case): fixed.\n- `MessageRowAvatarTests.swift:37` builds `thread(starter: \"Interlocuteurs multiples\")` with `isGroup` defaulting to `false`. The group state can only come from the label path of `avatarSubject`, which is the right case.\n\nNew findings:\n1. Detail: `MessageRowGroupHostedTests.swift:13-18` copies `listURL` and the parse helper from `MessageRowAvatarTests.swift:9-14`. Not blocking; a shared test helper would remove the copy.\n\nThe spec (#1158) is met: the value is set only when `avatarSubject(of:).isGroup`, the visible row is unchanged (#900), the hosted test exists, and the hand check with VoiceOver stays on #893.\n\n**Verified**\n- Read the diff `origin/dev-swift...884052d6`, the helpers it calls, the environment-value defaults, `MessageAvatarView`, and the issue.\n- `App/SwiftHFR.xcodeproj` uses folder-synchronized groups, so the new test file is in the test target without a project edit.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 3 changed files: 0 violations.\n- Not run: the app tests (no Xcode here). Compiling the hosted test and seeing it red then green is left to CI on macOS.\n\nNot marked ready: waiting for the Compile check on this head.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
